F repeat 2"},{"type":"Site","start":1081,"end":1082,"description":"Cleavage; by autolysis"},{"type":"Chain","start":1082,"end":2035,"description":"HCF C-terminal chain 2"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1101,"end":1126,"description":"HCF repeat 3"},{"type":"Site","start":1110,"end":1111,"description":"Cleavage; by autolysis"},{"type":"Chain","start":1111,"end":2035,"description":"HCF C-terminal chain 3"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1158,"end":1183,"description":"HCF repeat 4; degenerate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1205,"end":1205,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1219,"end":1219,"description":"Omega-N-methylarginine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1224,"end":1224,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1286,"end":1311,"description":"HCF repeat 5"},{"type":"Site","start":1295,"end":1296,"description":"Cleavage; by autolysis"},{"type":"Chain","start":1296,"end":2035,"description":"HCF C-terminal chain 4"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1314,"end":1339,"description":"HCF repeat 6"},{"type":"Site","start":1323,"end":1324,"description":"Cleavage; by autolysis"},{"type":"Chain","start":1324,"end":2035,"description":"HCF C-terminal chain 5"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1349,"end":1374,"description":"HCF repeat 7; degenerate"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1414,"end":1439,"description":"HCF repeat 8"},{"type":"Site","start":1423,"end":1424,"description":"Cleavage; by autolysis"},{"type":"Chain","start":1424,"end":2035,"description":"HCF C-terminal chain 6"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1491,"end":1491,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1497,"end":1497,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1507,"end":1507,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1771,"end":1771,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Domain","start":1797,"end":1888,"description":"Fibronectin type-III 2"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":1807,"end":1807,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":1808,"end":1808,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1838,"end":1838,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Domain","start":1890,"end":2006,"description":"Fibronectin type-III 3"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":2005,"end":2005,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":2024,"end":2024,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2)"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Composed predominantly of six polypeptides ranging from 110 to 150 kDa and a minor 300 kDa polypeptide (PubMed:10920196). The majority of N- and C-terminal cleavage products remain tightly, albeit non-covalently, associated (PubMed:10920196). Interacts with POU2F1, CREB3, ZBTB17, EGR2, E2F4, CREBZF, SP1, GABP2, Sin3 HDAC complex (SIN3A, HDAC1, HDAC2, SUDS3), SAP30, SIN3B and FHL2 (PubMed:10629049, PubMed:10675337, PubMed:10871379, PubMed:10976766, PubMed:10984507, PubMed:12244100, PubMed:12670868, PubMed:14532282, PubMed:15705566, PubMed:16624878, PubMed:9271389, PubMed:9389645). Component of a MLL1 complex, composed of at least the core components KMT2A/MLL1, ASH2L, HCFC1, WDR5 and RBBP5, as well as the facultative components BACC1, CHD8, DPY30, E2F6, HCFC2, HSP70, INO80C, KANSL1, LAS1L, MAX, MCRS1, MEN1, MGA, KAT8, PELP1, PHF20, PRP31, RING2, RUVBL1, RUVBL2, SENP3, TAF1, TAF4, TAF6, TAF7, TAF9 and TEX10 (PubMed:15199122, PubMed:15960975). Component of a THAP1/THAP3-HCFC1-OGT complex that is required for the regulation of the transcriptional activity of RRM1 (PubMed:20200153). Interacts directly with THAP3 (via its HBM) (PubMed:20200153). Interacts (via the Kelch-repeat domain) with THAP1 (via the HBM); the interaction recruits HCHC1 to the RRM1 (PubMed:20200153). Interacts with THAP7 and THAP11 (via the HMB) (PubMed:31905202). Interacts directly with OGT; the interaction, which requires the HCFC1 cleavage site domain, glycosylates and promotes the proteolytic processing of HCFC1, retains OGT in the nucleus and impacts the expression of herpes simplex virus immediate early viral genes (PubMed:12670868, PubMed:21285374, PubMed:23353889). Component of the SET1 complex, at least composed of the catalytic subunit (SETD1A or SETD1B), WDR5, WDR82, RBBP5, ASH2L, CXXC1, HCFC1 and DPY30 (PubMed:17998332, PubMed:18838538). Component of the NSL complex at least composed of MOF/KAT8, KANSL1, KANSL2, KANSL3, MCRS1, PHF20, OGT1/OGT, WDR5 and HCFC1 (PubMed:20018852). Component of a complex at least composed of ZNF335, HCFC1, CCAR2, EMSY, MKI67, RBBP5, ASH2L and WDR5; the complex is formed as a result of interactions between components of a nuclear receptor-mediated transcription complex and a histone methylation complex (PubMed:19131338). Within the complex interacts with ZNF335 (PubMed:19131338). Interacts with TET2 and TET3 (PubMed:23353889). Interacts with HCFC1R1 (PubMed:12235138). Interacts with THAP11 (By similarity). Interacts (via Kelch domain) with KMT2E/MLL5 isoform 3 (via HBM motif) (PubMed:23629655). Interacts with E2F1 (PubMed:23629655). Accessory scaffold component of the polycomb repressive deubiquitinase (PR-DUB) complex, at least composed of BAP1, one of ASXL1, ASXL2 or (probably) ASXL3 and one of MBD5 or MBD6; the PR-DUB core associates with a number of accessory proteins, including FOXK1, FOXK2, KDM1B, HCFC1, YY1 and OGT (PubMed:20805357, PubMed:30664650). Interacts with YY1 (via Gly-rich region); the interaction is direct (PubMed:20805357). Interacts with BAP1 (via HBM-like motif) (PubMed:19188440, PubMed:19815555, PubMed:20805357)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Associates with the VP16-induced complex; binding to HCFC1 activates the viral transcriptional activator VP16 for association with POU2F1, to form a multiprotein-DNA complex responsible for activating transcription of the viral immediate early genes (PubMed:10629049). Interacts with the viral transactivator protein VP16 (PubMed:10629049, PubMed:9271389, PubMed:9389645)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P51610-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Miscellaneous","text":"The N- and the C-terminal fragments fail to associate"}],"length":1966,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,381],[382,451,1585]],"edits":[{"start":382,"end":450,"original":"VSWGAVATADSYLLQLQKYDIPATAATATSPTPNPVPSVP","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":69,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":20,"foldedMissing":20,"features":[[1,69,0],[2,69,0],[3,69,0],[4,69,0],[5,69,0],[18,69,0],[19,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P51610-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P51610-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":46.4,"plddt":[[0,14],[50,1],[70,3],[90,5],[70,2],[90,25],[70,4],[90,25],[70,2],[90,9],[70,1],[90,10],[70,3],[90,25],[70,1],[90,28],[70,7],[90,13],[70,2],[50,2],[70,3],[90,24],[70,6],[90,10],[70,1],[90,48],[70,2],[50,3],[0,8],[50,1],[70,3],[90,16],[70,10],[90,13],[70,1],[90,9],[70,2],[50,3],[0,2],[50,3],[70,1],[90,10],[70,22],[50,4],[0,1],[50,8],[0,1344],[50,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,5],[50,1],[70,4],[90,5],[70,3],[50,3],[0,7],[50,4],[70,7],[90,3],[70,5],[90,6],[70,8],[90,3],[70,1],[90,1],[70,7],[50,2],[70,4],[90,1],[70,2],[90,4],[70,5],[90,6],[70,3],[50,4],[70,3],[90,7],[70,2],[50,2],[0,11],[50,2],[70,3],[90,14],[70,16],[90,7],[70,9],[90,5],[70,2],[50,2],[0,32]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"P51610-3","name":"3","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":428,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,427]],"edits":[{"start":428,"end":2035,"original":"PAPAAAAPAVQPLTQVGITLLPQAAPAPPTTTTIQVLPTV","replacement":"L","added":1}],"missing":1608,"replaced":0,"novel":1,"foldedAbsent":156,"foldedMissing":156,"features":[[1,592,0],[2,654,0],[3,683,0],[4,8